prompt:
A real photograph, taken with a good phone camera and looking exactly like a phone photograph, of the cobbled square in the middle of an old Berlin neighbourhood on a sunny Saturday afternoon in spring, taken as a person standing on the square a few metres away would take it, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, warm sunlight, a blue sky with a few white clouds. The textures of real stone, cobbles, brick, plaster, water, metal, wood, leaves, fabric and skin, with the true depth and the slight lens perspective of a photograph.

The first reference picture shows the young woman in three-quarter view, the second from the front: her face, her dark blonde hair tied back in a ponytail, her build and her height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; her clothes here are a light-green trench coat open over a white T-shirt, blue jeans and white sneakers, with a brown leather bag on her shoulder.

Every object stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. Nothing in the picture carries any writing, numbers or print: the shop fronts have no signs and no names, the church clock has a plain gold face with no numbers, the tram is plain yellow with no number and no words, the café umbrellas are plain white, the letterbox is plain yellow with no logo, and nothing carries a sign, a poster, a logo, a brand or a street name.

THE FRONT of the picture:
- a round stone fountain on the left, with water splashing from a small column in the middle into the basin;
- THE YOUNG WOMAN of the reference pictures sits on the stone edge of the fountain, seen whole from her head to her sneakers, which stand on the cobbles with their shadow beside them. She is caught in the very moment of eating an ice cream: she holds a cone with two scoops of pink and white ice cream in one hand and laughs at a small brown dog that sits in front of her and looks up at the ice cream;
- a pigeon walking on the cobbles near the fountain;
- a green metal waste bin on a post;
- a wooden bench with a black metal frame on the right.

THE MIDDLE of the picture:
- a small café terrace on the right with two round metal tables, metal chairs and a large plain white umbrella; at one table an old man of about seventy in a flat cap and a grey jacket reads a newspaper that shows only grey illegible lines, with a cup of coffee in front of him;
- a bronze statue of a man in a long coat standing on a tall stone pedestal in the middle of the square;
- a black street lamp;
- a few bicycles leaning against a metal rack;
- a young tree with fresh green leaves in a round metal grille.

THE BACK of the picture:
- an old brick church with a tall pointed tower and a round clock with a plain gold face and no numbers;
- a row of old five-storey houses painted cream, pale yellow and light pink, with tall windows and flower boxes of red geraniums, with shops on the ground floor that have plain awnings and no signs;
- a plain yellow tram with no number passing on the street behind the square;
- a traffic light at the corner of the street;
- a plain yellow letterbox on the wall of a house;
- a few pigeons flying in the blue sky with white clouds.
